  "status": "PASS",
  "summary": "Built the round-42 closure-suite limbs J12 (depth:density no-harm guard) and J13 (quiescence) as a sourceable bash file with sourceable entry points check_j12/check_j13, plus a raw transcript and a receipt. 40/40 graded assertions pass across 17 scenarios: both greens over the HEAD export (J12 deleted=0,density=1,base-density=1,missing=0,diff-read=ok exit 0; J13 clone=ok,ref=ok,uncommitted=0,drift=0,untracked=0,strays=0,leftovers=0,read=ok,scope=own exit 0) and 17 planted-failure scenarios each red with the expected payload value and exit 1.",
  "what_j12_asserts": "Deleted count = git --no-optional-locks -C <lane> diff --name-status --no-renames --diff-filter=D <base> <ref> -- corpus/ (pathspect corpus/ only, so E5's SKILL.md deletion is out of scope as the erratum directs; --no-renames so a corpus path renamed away counts as a deletion). Density = sha256 of TREE/corpus/instruments/density.py vs the re-derived sha256 of base:corpus/instruments/density.py, plus base-density checking that base blob's digest equals the pinned round-42 digest ee803726a3229eb924a6798fe0cf5309dacd33d42c40568da55d5c95f9f54710 (a wrong base reds rather than passes). missing=1 when the file is absent. diff-read=fail on any failed git call. renamed is diagnostic only and does not gate.",
  "what_j13_asserts": "Quiescence measured in a clone of the lane BOUND TO THE EXPORTED REF BY NAME: clone --shared --no-checkout into the run's own --work (toplevel asserted), cat-file -e $ref (unresolvable ref is a distinct red, never a vacuous tally), update-ref --no-deref HEAD $ref + read-tree $ref so the clone's HEAD and index become the ref's tree and the exported tree becomes its work tree. Three independent counters of the same property: uncommitted (git status --porcelain line count, the literal 'no uncommitted changes in a clone of the exported ref' reading), drift (git diff --name-status), untracked (git ls-files --others, counted WITHOUT standard excludes so ignored extras count too). Scratch scan rooted at the run's --scratch-root (never host-global per E4): strays counts kasegi-r4[0-9]* family matches (case/separator-insensitive, leading dots stripped, separators folded to '-'), leftovers counts EVERY other non---work entry so a leftover seat dir reds as E4 requires. --work subtree pruned so the run's own artifacts are never counted. Tolerance: --work, its contents, and a clean-chain ancestor; a family symlink resolving to an ancestor of --work is never tolerated (round-40 wave-2 F5 escape). scope=host-global (caller passed /fast/scratch/hyaku) is RED, as is a --work outside the scanned root; both fail closed.",
  "lane_safety": "Only read-only git against the lane (diff, cat-file, rev-parse, archive, clone --shared --no-checkout). The lane's .git directory is byte-identical before and after the whole run (d64631cf285f689e887ae0862ddabcaf1f885ee51aa51e7bcd119bb232a64767). The clone lives under the run's own --work, never in the lane, and is deleted before the function returns. git status --porcelain shows 0 tracked modifications; corpus/ D rows base..HEAD = 0; density.py at HEAD = ee803726a3229eb924a6798fe0cf5309dacd33d42c40568da55d5c95f9f54710.",
  "defects_found_and_fixed_in_my_limb": {
    "item": [
      "Scan resolved entries with cd, which fails on plain regular files and counted the J13 clone's own .git files as strays (strays=26 on a clean scratch) -> fixed with realpath -m plus pruning the --work subtree.",
      "J13_LANE was ignored because check_j13 read the lane through the J12 accessor -> j12j13_lane now takes the override variable name and check_j13 passes J13_LANE.",
      "Default lane derivation assumed a fixed depth (file/../..), wrong when the limb sits in a wave dir -> now walks up to the nearest enclosing git work tree.",
      "F5 symlink escape was not distinguished: a family symlink resolving to an ancestor of --work was tolerated when the chain below happened to be clean -> symlinks to ancestors are now never tolerated.",
      "The probe's host-global case walked the real /fast/scratch/hyaku (>1e6 entries), slow and contrary to the never-host-global rule -> J13_FLEET_ROOT is redirected at the probe's own tree so the case is hermetic."
    ]
  },
  "defect_in_my_test_not_the_limb": "The planted missing-file case removed SKORECARD.md (typo) instead of SCORECARD.md, so the tree was never mutated and the case correctly reported green. Typo fixed; the case now reds as designed. Flagged because it is the same shape of error the round-42 kill rule targets: a 'failure' fixture that does not actually plant the failure.",
  "integration_notes_for_L1": {
    "item": [
      "Source ExecJ12J13.sh; call check_j12 $EXPORT $REF and check_j13 $EXPORT $REF; each prints one payload line and returns 0 green / 1 red.",
      "Set BASE_REF=5053a7f46de35784cff4b56756906e9014a38276 (or J12_BASE) and SCRATCH_ROOT to the run's own scratch root.",
      "WORK must lie INSIDE SCRATCH_ROOT, else J13 fails closed by design.",
      "At receipt time the scratch root must be free of leftover seat dirs and kasegi-r4[0-9]* entries other than this run's own --work (E4: that cleanup is the check's job).",
      "Suggested graded-selftest needles: J12 deleted=1, density=0, missing=1, base-density=0; J13 uncommitted=1, drift=1, untracked=1, strays=1, leftovers=1, ref=fail, scope=host-global, read=fail. Assert payload value AND exit status (E8: J12/J13 have no committed defeat artifact, so graded mutants are the required negative evidence).",
      "Do NOT point SCRATCH_ROOT at /fast/scratch/hyaku: J13 reports scope=host-global and reds."
    ]
  },
  "residual_risks": {
    "item": [
      "J13's scratch scan is a live measurement and is red whenever the scratch root holds anything beyond this run's --work. That is E4's specified behaviour, but it makes the check sensitive to the L1's cleanup discipline at receipt time.",
      "renamed in the J12 payload does not gate (deleted does). One-line change if the L1 prefers both to gate, but it would double-count the same defect.",
      "The J13 clone borrows the lane's object store via --shared alternates; an intervening lane gc could make it fail closed (ref=fail/read=fail) rather than false-green. Negligible within one suite run.",
      "The lane HEAD advanced three times while this seat worked (27e18d2 erratum-1, 8be06a9 erratum-2, 514ff62). The transcript records the ref measured against (514ff62d61ee9bc717a20a02a22c65ec0c5124ed); the limb is ref-agnostic and reads the ref it is given, but the graded selftest should be run against the final Y ref when the suite lands."
    ]
  },
  "host_guard_compliance": {
    "item": [
      "Only the two deliverables plus this receipt were written in the lane; no other lane, fleet, sibling-lane or source tree file was written.",
      "No mutating git/jj command was run anywhere (no add/commit/push/checkout/reset/stash, no jj mutating subcommand). Fixture repos for the J12 deletion/rename scenarios were built with git init inside the seat's own scratch dir with the toplevel asserted before every commit, per the host guard.",
      "Scratch dir /fast/scratch/hyaku/kasegi-r42/ExecJ12J13 was removed before yielding; TMPDIR was bound to it for every command.",
      "Disk guard was green (disk-guard.sh status exit 0) before the work; no heavy pass was run while it was not.",
      "No package was installed; the limb uses only existing git 2.56.0 and coreutils.",
      "No subagent was spawned (leaf seat; the one allowed labrat probe was not needed)."
    ]
  },
  "verification_performed_by_this_seat": {
    "item": [
      "Full probe matrix re-run from the DELIVERED limb file after all fixes: probe cases=40 failures=0, exit 0.",
      "Suite-simulation sourcing test with only the suite globals set (LANE, BASE_REF, WORK, SCRATCH_ROOT): J12 closed=1, J13 closed=1, closed=2/2 exit=0; sourcing alone produces empty output.",
      "Lane integrity: 0 tracked modifications, 0 corpus D rows base..HEAD, density.py digest at HEAD matches the pinned value, lane .git byte-identical before/after.",
      "Scratch dir confirmed absent after cleanup."
    ]
  },
  "note_on_unrelated_inbound_message": "An inbound IRC message from TsukuroiR48 asked that .ufo/waves/round-48/w1.ready be removed/ignored. That concerns round-48 in a different lane and is outside this seat's write scope (kasegi round 42); no action was taken."
