  "behavior": "Instrument QA seat. Built and validated a scratch git mirror preserving the lane's real commit hashes (5053a7f4.../1f746461.../0566bd66...) so --export-ref resolves to the exact hashes the frozen claims name, plus a driver running 6 baseline suite runs (selftest at tip, run at tip/base/r41-head, plain-run refusal, unresolvable-ref red) and 7 mutants, each on a fresh fixture commit with its own git index and its own isolated --scratch-root/--work. Measured every mutant against the LANDED J-limbs (the same check_jN entry points the r42 suite sources): J5 mutant REJECTED (pristine closed=1 -> mutant closed=0, strays=2/outside=1); J11 duplication detected (corrections 31->57, dups 4->5, dup-lines 4->30); F-FLIP status-flip ACCEPTED (escape); J12 INCONCLUSIVE (limb red on the pristine fixture too, diff-read=fail, driver limitation not a J12 defect). The r42 suite deliverable ExecSuiteCore.r42-closure.sh never landed (~2h polling), so the two assigned suite-level runs were NOT executed and NO transcript was fabricated for them.",
