    },
    {
      "id": "F-BIND-DELIVERABLE-IS-UNPATCHED",
      "severity": "high",
      "detail": ".ufo/waves/round-42/wave1/ExecJ6Bind.capture-binding-check.py is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the committed corpus/instruments/capture-binding-check.py (both sha256 3d9e5e0ddbaaccf91db255b4a978d49a1d44a2c54cd7cc1fef22c78330da99fa, 892 lines / 40556 bytes). It therefore carries no capture-existence rule: deleting corpus/source-snapshots/round-41/S063.txt while keeping the manifest record's path still prints records=55 bound=55 unbound=0 exit=0 (the MutBindingExistence.md defeat survives). The sibling URL case-flip IS rejected (rule=url-mismatch, bound=54, exit=1)."
    },
    {
      "id": "J5-OUTSIDE-SCAN-RECURSIVE",
      "severity": "medium",
      "detail": "J5's outside limb counts family-shaped entries recursively under the scope parent, so a scope containing a sibling export tree (which carries tracked .ufo/waves/round-4*/kasegi-r4*-*.ready files) reads outside=82 on a PRISTINE fixture. Any counting command sharing a --scratch-root parent will read red for environmental reasons."
