  "behavior": "The C2 junk twin control named in the round-42 kill rule ('a mined-marked row without capture+entry+harness pass — the O4 class') is fabricated on scratch copies of the lane corpus and every named instrument is run against the mutated copy. The twin is a mined registry row S999 whose used-by names a knowledge file that does not exist, plus an F25-lookalike frontier row naming a missing entry, plus a snapshot manifest that claims S999 with no url, no fetch provenance and no capture bytes — and no entry, no capture file, no harness pass. A monotone ladder of nine arms (base, J1..J6, P5, LIVE-J3) measures the rejection at each layer, cut from both the claims' frozen base (5053a7f, corpus byte-identical to the freeze commit) and a copy of the live lane working tree. On the full O4 twin (J3) and on its live-tree replay (LIVE-J3) ALL THREE named instruments reject it independently: frontier-recheck-count.py exit 1 (FAIL F25 problems=missing-entry, entries=28 pass=27), capture-binding-check.py exit 1 (FAIL rule=url-mismatch record=S999 detail=absent, FAIL rule=provenance-missing, records=56 bound=55 unbound=1), sources-census.sh validate exit 1 (E11 S999 missing used-by). No instrument is load-bearing alone: J5 blinds the census's E11 limb (used-by set to the em-dash, so the census prints only W03) and the frontier harness and capture-binding check still reject with exit 1 each; J6 shows the harness rejecting on its recheck limb (problems=recheck-exit-2) rather than its missing-entry limb; J4 shows the census alone going green once the used-by path exists while the other two still red. The recheck-audit is a fourth independent rejection on the arms that write a knowledge file (J4/J6 read unexpected=1 exit=1). The C2 measure conjunct reads criterion met=no on every O4-class arm. The counting-command ledger shows the twin SATISFIES the two raw row-count greps (frontier 25, registry 64) while failing the other seven, so the after-state is reachable only as a conjunction, never by row-count arithmetic. P5 is reported as a labelled boundary probe outside the O4 class (a self-consistent forgery — forged capture, manifest, entry, recheck line and expected-list line — is green on all three instruments), which is the honest edge of the local guard and not a claim defect.",
  "evidence": "Commands actually run (all with their actual output recorded in ExecControls.junk-recheck.txt): 'bash /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/hyaku/disk-guard.sh status' green before the heavy pass (/fast/scratch/hyaku 27% used, 592.6G free); 'git -C <lane> archive 5053a7f46de35784cff4b56756906e9014a38276 | tar -x -C <scratch>/master' for the frozen base (git diff --stat <base> HEAD -- corpus is empty, so the corpus is byte-identical to the freeze commit); 'tar -C <lane> --exclude=.git --exclude=.jj -cf - . | tar -C <scratch>/master-live -xf -' for the live tree; per arm the three named instruments plus recheck-audit.py, source-recheck.py on the junk manifest, the census and every C2 counting command verbatim; 'bash ExecControls.replay.sh <scratch>' verified from its delivered location — it reproduces the same three rejections and exits 0. Harm check: landing junk-f25.md at .ufo/waves/round-42/c2-controls/ was byte-identical on every counter and instrument before and after ('VERDICT: instrument outputs byte-identical before/after the landing = YES'); both fabricated rows are indented four spaces so grep -c '^|' on the landed file returns 0. Live positive control after the seat's work: harness entries=27 pass=27 exit=0, binding records=55 bound=55 unbound=0, census exit=0. 'git status --porcelain -- corpus/' is empty — no corpus file was written. No mutating git/jj command was run anywhere.",
